; The OCaml side of the development. Nothing is built from this directory
; itself; it exists to hold the extraction and the libraries, and to stop
; the parent theory's (include_subdirs qualified) recursion — without the
; stanza below, the RocqBottom theory would try to claim extraction/
; extract.v as one of its modules and dune would abort on directory load.
;
;   extraction/PrimitiveExtraction.v: Rocq primitives -> OCaml primitives
;   extraction/driver/       the single (coq.extraction)
;   abstractioncombination/  \
;   quadrivalent/             |  one library per node of the Rocq module
;   tf_quadrivalent/          |
;   zinterval/                |  graph, each owning the modules it defines
;   tf_zinterval/            /   and copying them out of extraction/driver
;
; Each library's .ml/.mli are checked in and are the deliverable: they
; build without Rocq. `dune build` refreshes them in place via
; (copy_files (mode promote)), so a proof change that alters a transfer
; function shows up as a plain `git diff` (no need for manual calls
; to dune promote).
(include_subdirs no)
